2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  CLAIM    T0317 encrypted ("mango") media needs a content-rights call and an AES-128-CTR decrypt, and the mp3-only selection is retired
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  CHANGE   src/suno/MangoCrypto.{hpp,cpp}: gcmDecrypt() (AES-GCM, 16- or 32-byte key, 12-byte nonce, 16-byte tag, AAD = the clip id) and ctrCrypt() / CtrStream (AES-CTR, 128-bit big-endian counter).
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  CHANGE   The AES block cipher comes from libavutil (av_aes_init/av_aes_crypt, ECB), so no new native dependency is needed on any of the three platforms. cmake/Dependencies.cmake probes for that exact API by COMPILING it (check_cxx_source_compiles) rather than by version, because libavutil's AES entry points changed shape: av_aes_init() took the key from FFmpeg 5.1 onwards and did not before.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  CHANGE   The probe is re-run on every configure: a FAILED check_cxx_source_compiles is cached as an empty entry, so one bad configure would have switched the feature off permanently.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  CHANGE   Without the AES API the file compiles to a stub that reports itself unavailable at runtime -- the same shape as the burn-in's CHADVIS_HAS_AVFILTER gate, and the same reason: an optional feature must not break the build of an unrelated one.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  VERIFY   unit_tests -> "[suite] TestMangoCrypto -> 0", 18 assertions. ctest --test-dir build-fast/tests -j3 -> 100% tests passed, 0 failed out of 14, 87.61 s.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  VERIFY   The vectors are TWO independent anchors, because one is not enough: the published NIST SP 800-38D cases 1-4 (empty, one block, 64-byte ciphertext, 20-byte AAD + 60-byte ciphertext) and vectors generated by WebCrypto -- the same primitive the server's own browser client uses -- whose generator DECRYPTS each one before emitting it, so a corrupt constant cannot reach the test.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  VERIFY   The AES-CTR path is pinned against WebCrypto byte-for-byte, and CtrStream is checked at 40 different chunk sizes, because a streamed body is read in whatever sizes the filesystem hands over.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  NOTE     Two real bugs were found and fixed while writing this, and both are the kind a passing build would have hidden. (1) The GHASH accumulator was multiplied as H times H instead of the accumulator times H, and the multiply aliased its input -- every tag was wrong, and the first symptom was that a 16-byte license "verified". (2) The AAD and the ciphertext were absorbed as one concatenated buffer; the spec pads the AAD to a block boundary FIRST, and the clip id is 36 bytes, so it is always a partial block -- a wrong tag on every real license. A third failure was in the test fixture itself: a hand-copied hex constant that WebCrypto could not even decrypt.
2026-10-22T04:10:00Z  NOT-VERIFIED  The GCM tag check is verified against NIST and WebCrypto, but no real server license has been unwrapped by this code yet -- the end-to-end run (rights call -> decrypt -> playable file) is the next slice.
